\ rill/rt.4 - the command model's runtime (873): Rill's (736-870), kept when Rill was retired - values in an
\ arena and its collector, texts, lists and maps, processes and pipelines, the environment, globs; the boot
\ word. At 873 its genes fixed at their defaults (the constants below; rill/genes.tsv and tools/rill-genes.py
\ gone with Rill's search) and the words nothing of the command model reaches taken out - Rill's library,
\ JSON, jobs' extras, the range and slice forms: in git before 873. Its messages say cm.
\ ---- the shell's own output, into $( )'s text when one is being made (896) ---------------------------
\ TYPE is the engine's: to fd 1, through its buffer. While CT-ON, what the command model prints - echo,
\ values nobody takes - is added to CT-BUF instead, the text a $( ) is making: no file, no descriptor
\ (a temporary file each had made calls 100 times slower). OUT-TYPE and OUT-EMIT, not TYPE and EMIT
\ defined again: the words that print the command model's output use them - SHOW's, ECHO, R-NL, R-TYPE.
\ Errors (R-ERR>) and output redirected to a file (RD-RUN, a function stage's file) put it off while they
\ write; a program's pipeline, its stdout not redirected, is read into it (PL-BEGIN 2, PIPE-END).
VARIABLE CT-ON   VARIABLE CT-BUF   VARIABLE CT-LEN   VARIABLE CT-CAP   VARIABLE CT-WAS
: CT+ ( c-addr u --- )
  DUP CT-LEN @ +  DUP CT-CAP @ > IF  2* 4096 MAX DUP CT-CAP !  CT-BUF @ ?DUP IF SWAP RESIZE ELSE ALLOCATE THEN THROW CT-BUF !
  ELSE DROP THEN  CT-BUF @ CT-LEN @ + SWAP DUP CT-LEN +! MOVE ;
: OUT-TYPE ( c-addr u --- )   CT-ON @ IF CT+ ELSE TYPE THEN ;
: OUT-EMIT ( c --- )   SP@ 1 OUT-TYPE DROP ;
4 CONSTANT G-LISTCAP   4 CONSTANT G-GROWTH   16 CONSTANT G-RECHASH
\ rill/rt.4 - Rill's runtime, stage 1a (Iteration 736): text values in an
\ arena, joining them, and the boot word of Rill's image. Loaded after
\ the Forth libraries the shell's image also loads (SHELL-LANGUAGE.md
\ Part 5); none of relfsh's own sources.
\
\ A text value is one cell: the address of a cell holding its length,
\ its bytes after it. Numbers are cells. The arena is one block, bumped
\ and never freed piecemeal: a script's values live until it ends.

VARIABLE R-TOP   VARIABLE R-END
VARIABLE R-ARENA0  VARIABLE R-GC-AT  VARIABLE G-STRESS   \ the arena's start; where the next collection is due (776)
134217728 CONSTANT R-ARENA-SIZE
: R-ARENA-INIT ( --- )   R-ARENA-SIZE ALLOCATE THROW  DUP R-ARENA0 !  DUP R-TOP !  DUP R-ARENA-SIZE + R-END !  16777216 + R-GC-AT ! ;   \ 128 MB of address space, touched only as used (755: 16 MB filled by the pilot)
DEFER R-FULL   \ the arena full: R-FULL-IMPL below says why, and where (791)
: R-ALLOT ( n --- addr )
  7 + -8 AND  R-TOP @ SWAP OVER + DUP R-END @ U> IF R-FULL THEN  R-TOP ! ;   \ the test a branch, its message only when full (768)
: R-TEXT ( c-addr u --- t )   DUP CELL+ R-ALLOT >R  DUP R@ !  R@ CELL+ SWAP MOVE  R> ;
: R-T@ ( t --- c-addr u )   DUP CELL+ SWAP @ ;
VARIABLE RB-T

: R-NUM ( n --- t )   DUP ABS 0 <# #S ROT SIGN #> R-TEXT ;
VARIABLE RC-N   VARIABLE RC-T   VARIABLE RC-P
: R-CONCAT ( t1 .. tn n --- t )   \ n texts joined, the deepest first
  RC-N !  0  RC-N @ 0 ?DO  I 1+ PICK @ +  LOOP
  DUP CELL+ R-ALLOT TUCK ! RC-T !
  RC-T @ DUP @ + CELL+ RC-P !
  RC-N @ 0 ?DO  R-T@ DUP NEGATE RC-P +!  RC-P @ SWAP MOVE  LOOP
  RC-T @ ;
: R-TCMP ( t1 t2 --- n )   >R R-T@ R> R-T@ COMPARE ;   \ texts in order, by their bytes: Python's order for UTF-8 (786)
: R-TYPE ( t --- )   R-T@ OUT-TYPE ;
: R-NL ( --- )   10 OUT-EMIT ;

\ ---- Lists and records (stage 2, Iteration 739) -------------------------
\ An item of a list or a field of a record is a box: two cells, its kind
\ and its value - the one place values of different kinds meet (Part 5).
\ A list is [count][capacity][items], the items a cell array of boxes; a
\ record the same with a key array beside it, each key a text. Both grow
\ by a new array twice the size, the old one left in the arena.
: /STRING ( c-addr u n --- c-addr' u' )   TUCK - >R + R> ;   \ not in the kernel
1 CONSTANT K-NUM   2 CONSTANT K-TEXT   3 CONSTANT K-BOOL   4 CONSTANT K-LIST   5 CONSTANT K-REC   \ 6 was Rill's decimal (923)
VARIABLE RL   VARIABLE RJ-SEP
: R-BOX ( v kind --- box )   2 CELLS R-ALLOT >R  R@ !  R@ CELL+ !  R> ;   \ boxsmall tried and taken out (752)
: R-UNBOX ( box --- v kind )   DUP CELL+ @ SWAP @ ;
\ ---- Where a run-time error happened (Iteration 781) -----------------------
\ Each statement of the script marks, as its code is compiled ([ n R-MARK ]
\ - nothing at run time), where its code starts and its line. An error looks
\ down the return stack for the innermost address in the script's own code:
\ above the first mark, below HERE. The table lives in the C heap. Gene lines.
VARIABLE MK-A  VARIABLE MK-N  VARIABLE MK-CAP

: R-MARK ( n --- )   \ between [ and ], as a statement is compiled (back at 887: the command model's too)
  MK-N @ MK-CAP @ = IF
    MK-CAP @ 2* 256 MAX DUP MK-CAP !  2* CELLS  MK-A @ ?DUP IF SWAP RESIZE ELSE ALLOCATE THEN THROW MK-A ! THEN
  HERE  MK-A @ MK-N @ 2* CELLS + 2!  1 MK-N +! ;
: MK-LINE ( a --- n )   \ the line whose code holds a; 0: not the script's code
  MK-N @ 0= IF DROP 0 EXIT THEN
  DUP MK-A @ @ U< IF DROP 0 EXIT THEN
  DUP HERE U< 0= IF DROP 0 EXIT THEN
  0 SWAP  MK-N @ 0 ?DO  DUP MK-A @ I 2* CELLS + @ U< IF LEAVE THEN  NIP MK-A @ I 2* CELLS + CELL+ @ SWAP  LOOP DROP ;
\ Rill's own messages go to the err port (821): an error is not the script's output - `x = $(a-script)`
\ took one as its value. At an error's first word, R-ERR>: the engine's output buffer flushed (the WRITE
\ primitive flushes it first - a write of nothing; WRITE-FILE writes nothing for nothing, so does not
\ get there), the real stdout kept on a spare fd, fd 1 pointed at fd 2 - so all
\ of the message, its line included, goes there. R-BOOT puts stdout back before on EXIT runs.
VARIABLE R-OUT-KEPT                       \ the real stdout while an error is told; 0, none
: R-ERR> ( --- )
  R-OUT-KEPT @ IF EXIT THEN  CT-ON @ CT-WAS !  0 CT-ON !          \ an error is not $( )'s text (896)
  PAD 0 1 WRITE DROP  1 10 DUP-FROM DUP 0< IF DROP EXIT THEN  R-OUT-KEPT !  2 1 DUP2 DROP ;
: R-OUT-BACK ( --- )
  R-OUT-KEPT @ ?DUP 0= IF EXIT THEN  PAD 0 1 WRITE DROP  1 DUP2 DROP  R-OUT-KEPT @ CLOSE-FILE DROP  0 R-OUT-KEPT !
  CT-WAS @ CT-ON ! ;
DEFER R-LINE. ( n --- )   \ "line n" - the command model's says the file, for a sourced one's (890)
: R-LINE-N. ( n --- )   ." line " 0 <# #S #> TYPE ;   ' R-LINE-N. IS R-LINE.
: R-WHERE ( --- )   \ " (line n)", the innermost of the script's statements running
  R0 @ RP@ ?DO  I @ MK-LINE ?DUP IF ."  (" R-LINE. ." )" UNLOOP EXIT THEN  1 CELLS +LOOP ;
: R-ERR-NL ( --- )   R-WHERE R-NL ;
: R-FAIL ( c-addr u --- )   R-ERR> TYPE R-ERR-NL -4004 THROW ;   \ a Rill error: its message, its line, status 2 - not ABORT", which
\ A stack in a BUFFER: grows when full (891): its space moved to the heap, twice as big, what it held
\ copied, and the BUFFER:'s descriptor pointed at it, so every use of its name finds the new space. Each had
\ a most - captures 64 deep (recursion through $( ) stopped there), blocks and activations 256, jobs 16.
\ A body is kept as an offset from START: the image is saved and reloaded.
: BODY-OF ( offset --- body )   START @ + ;
\ Recursion's depth: the return stack holds 64 KB (RSTACK_BYTES in engine/cv8.c). Its guard page stops a
\ plain call that runs past it, but one inside a CATCH - a def with return, a capture, a block - came back to
\ frames in the runaway region and crashed (891, once the 256 activations and 64 captures that had stopped it
\ sooner were gone). So each of those says it while there is room to unwind.
: R-DEEP? ( --- )   R0 @ RP@ - 60000 > IF S" cm: recursion too deep for the stacks" R-FAIL THEN ;
: BUF-GROW ( body --- )
  >R  R@ CELL+ @ 2*  DUP ALLOCATE IF S" cm: out of memory" R-FAIL THEN      ( size' new )
  R@ @ OVER R@ CELL+ @ MOVE  R@ @ IN-ARENA? 0= IF R@ @ FREE DROP THEN  R@ !  R> CELL+ ! ;
                                                            \ added the word it was in, then `cm: error -2`, no line (818)
: R-.N ( n --- )   DUP ABS 0 <# #S ROT SIGN #> TYPE ;   \ a number, no blank after: before " (line n)" (799)
\ ---- Checked arithmetic (Iteration 794): past 64 bits, or a division by zero
\ is an error naming the line, not a wrapped number or the engine's trap. 1+ and 1- stay plain: counting cannot get there.
: R-OVF ( --- )   R-ERR> ." cm: a number past 64 bits - whole numbers are -9223372036854775808 to 9223372036854775807" R-ERR-NL -4008 THROW ;
: R-ZDIV ( --- )   R-ERR> ." cm: division by zero" R-ERR-NL -4008 THROW ;
: R-ADD ( a b --- c )   2DUP + >R  R@ XOR SWAP R@ XOR AND 0< IF R> DROP R-OVF THEN R> ;
: R-MINUS ( a b --- c )   2DUP - >R  OVER XOR  SWAP R@ XOR  AND 0< IF R> DROP R-OVF THEN R> ;
: R-MUL ( a b --- c )   M*  OVER 0< IF DUP -1 <> ELSE DUP 0<> THEN NIP IF DROP R-OVF THEN ;
: R-DIV ( a b --- c )   DUP 0= IF R-ZDIV THEN  / ;
: R-MODC ( a b --- c )   DUP 0= IF R-ZDIV THEN  MOD ;
\ ---- the arena in chunks (918): full where nothing may be collected - in a def a capture called, its loop
\ building a long text - it grows: the chunk it fills kept as it is, a new one taken, the next collection
\ copying what is live in all of them into one. 128 MB had been the most; now the machine's memory is
VARIABLE XN   VARIABLE XC-P   VARIABLE XC-CAP      \ chunks filled since the last collection: [start][end][bits] each
: X-CHUNK ( i --- addr )   3 * CELLS XC-P @ + ;
: R-OOM ( --- )   R-ERR> ." cm: out of memory - the machine has no more for the arena" R-ERR-NL -4006 THROW ;
: R-NEW-CHUNK ( n --- )   \ the chunk being filled kept, filled to R-TOP; a new one, n bytes at least, the arena's size at least
  XN @ XC-CAP @ = IF  XC-CAP @ 2* 8 MAX DUP XC-CAP !  3 * CELLS XC-P @ ?DUP IF SWAP RESIZE ELSE ALLOCATE THEN IF R-OOM THEN XC-P !  THEN
  R-ARENA0 @ XN @ X-CHUNK !  R-TOP @ XN @ X-CHUNK CELL+ !  1 XN +!
  R-ARENA-SIZE MAX  DUP ALLOCATE IF R-OOM THEN                ( size a )
  DUP R-ARENA0 !  DUP R-TOP !  + R-END !  R-TOP @ R-GC-AT ! ;  \ collected at the next safe point
: R-FULL-IMPL ( old new --- old' new' )   OVER - NIP  DUP 2* 65536 + R-NEW-CHUNK  R-TOP @ TUCK + ;
' R-FULL-IMPL IS R-FULL
: R-READ-GROW ( t p --- t' p' )   \ a program's output outgrew the chunk: what is read so far moved to a new one
  OVER - >R  R@ 2* 65536 + R-NEW-CHUNK  R-TOP @ R@ MOVE  R-TOP @ DUP R> + ;

: R-KIND-ERR ( --- )   R-ERR> ." cm: a value of the wrong kind" R-ERR-NL  -4001 THROW ;
: R-ANY>NUM ( box --- n )   R-UNBOX DUP K-NUM = OVER K-BOOL = OR 0= IF R-KIND-ERR THEN DROP ;

DEFER R-CONT>TEXT-D   \ a list's or a record's text: R-CONT>TEXT, below (793)
: R-ANY>TEXT ( box --- t )
  R-UNBOX  DUP K-TEXT = IF DROP EXIT THEN
  DUP K-NUM = IF DROP R-NUM EXIT THEN
  DUP K-BOOL = IF DROP IF S" true" ELSE S" false" THEN R-TEXT EXIT THEN
  R-CONT>TEXT-D ;                                              \ a list or a record (793: it left the value under its text)
: R-NEW-LIST ( --- l )   3 CELLS R-ALLOT  0 OVER !  G-LISTCAP OVER CELL+ !  G-LISTCAP CELLS R-ALLOT OVER 2 CELLS + ! ;   \ genes 749
: R-LEN ( l --- n )   @ ;
: R-ITEMS ( l --- a )   2 CELLS + @ ;
: R-GROW ( l --- )   \ room for one more item
  DUP @ OVER CELL+ @ < IF DROP EXIT THEN
  DUP CELL+ @ DUP G-GROWTH * 2/ SWAP 1+ MAX DUP CELLS R-ALLOT     ( l cap2 a2 )   \ capacity * growth / 2, at least one more
  >R OVER R-ITEMS R@ 3 PICK @ CELLS MOVE         \ the items copied
  OVER CELL+ !  R> SWAP 2 CELLS + ! ;
: R-PUSH ( box l --- )   DUP @ OVER CELL+ @ < 0= IF DUP R-GROW THEN  DUP >R  2 CELLS + @ R@ @ CELLS + !  1 R> +! ;   \ R-GROW only when full (775)
: R-INDEX ( l i --- l i' )   \ an index the unsigned test refused: from the end when negative and in the list,
  \ as Python's $l[-1] (771); past either end an error. Reached only where the plain read would fail.
  DUP 0< IF OVER @ OVER + DUP 0< 0= IF NIP EXIT THEN DROP THEN
  R-ERR> ." cm: index " . ." past a list of " @ R-.N R-ERR-NL -4002 THROW ;
: R-AT ( l i --- box )   OVER @ OVER U> 0= IF R-INDEX THEN  CELLS SWAP 2 CELLS + @ + @ ;
