\ Commands, pipelines, output captured, ports redirected (stage 1b,
\ Iteration 738). Rill's own executor on the kernel's FORK, EXECVE,
\ WAITPID, PIPE and DUP2 - nothing of the shell's. A program is found on
\ PATH by env, one exec more, until the search is written in Forth.
: R-CSTR ( t --- c-addr )   R-T@ DUP 1+ R-ALLOT >R  TUCK R@ SWAP MOVE  R@ + 0 SWAP C!  R> ;
\ setenv(name, value) (783): for env(name), and for every command Rill runs from then on - each
\ gets NAME=value from env, which starts them all. The NAME=value strings live in the C heap.
VARIABLE SE-P  VARIABLE SE-CAP   VARIABLE SE-N   VARIABLE SE-B   VARIABLE SE-U   \ setenv's names: in the heap, grown
: SE-A ( --- a )   SE-P @ ;                        \ as they come (907: 32 at most before); each NAME=value or --unset=NAME
: SE-ROOM ( --- )   SE-N @ SE-CAP @ < IF EXIT THEN  SE-CAP @ 2* 16 MAX DUP SE-CAP !  CELLS SE-P @ ?DUP IF SWAP RESIZE ELSE ALLOCATE THEN THROW SE-P ! ;
: SE-UNSET? ( e --- f )   DUP CSTRLEN 8 MIN S" --unset=" COMPARE 0= ;
: SE-MATCH? ( a u e --- f )   \ the C string e is NAME=... for the name a u - or --unset=NAME
  DUP SE-UNSET? IF  8 + DUP CSTRLEN COMPARE 0= EXIT  THEN
  >R  R@ CSTRLEN OVER > 0= IF 2DROP R> DROP 0 EXIT THEN
  DUP R@ + C@ [CHAR] = <> IF 2DROP R> DROP 0 EXIT THEN
  R> OVER COMPARE 0= ;
: SE-FIND ( a u --- i )   SE-N @ 0 ?DO 2DUP I CELLS SE-A + @ SE-MATCH? IF 2DROP I UNLOOP EXIT THEN LOOP 2DROP -1 ;
: R-SETENV ( name value --- )
  SWAP R-T@ ROT R-T@                                       ( na nu va vu )
  2 PICK OVER + 2 + ALLOCATE THROW SE-B !
  2SWAP DUP SE-U !  SE-B @ SWAP MOVE                      ( va vu )
  [CHAR] = SE-B @ SE-U @ + C!
  DUP >R SE-B @ SE-U @ 1+ + SWAP MOVE  0 SE-B @ SE-U @ 1+ R> + + C!
  SE-B @ SE-U @ SE-FIND DUP 0< IF
    DROP SE-ROOM  SE-N @ 1 SE-N +!
  ELSE DUP CELLS SE-A + @ FREE DROP THEN
  CELLS SE-A + SE-B @ SWAP ! ;
