\ Jobs (Iteration 813, QUESTIONS.md A36): spawn((cmd)) starts a pipeline and does not wait - its stdin
\ /dev/null unless redirected, as POSIX has it for & - and returns its last stage's pid; wait(job)
\ waits for its stages and gives the pipeline's status, as PL-END makes it; a job not waited for gets
\ TERM when the script ends (R-BOOT, after on EXIT), not waited for in turn - init reaps it. A script
\ that spawns catches INT and TERM, so that it ends through R-BOOT and its jobs with it. The table
\ is compact - JB-N entries, the last moved into a freed one - so a BUFFER:'s first bytes never count.
16 CONSTANT JB-MAX
JB-MAX CELLS BUFFER: JB-KEY   JB-MAX CELLS BUFFER: JB-NP   JB-MAX PL-MAX * CELLS BUFFER: JB-PIDS   VARIABLE JB-N
VARIABLE JB-CAP  JB-MAX JB-CAP !                   \ grown when full (891): the three tables together, rows kept
' JB-KEY >BODY START @ - CONSTANT JB-KEY'   ' JB-NP >BODY START @ - CONSTANT JB-NP'   ' JB-PIDS >BODY START @ - CONSTANT JB-PIDS'
: JB-MORE ( --- )   JB-KEY' BODY-OF BUF-GROW  JB-NP' BODY-OF BUF-GROW  JB-PIDS' BODY-OF BUF-GROW  JB-CAP @ 2* JB-CAP ! ;
: JB-PID ( slot i --- addr )   SWAP PL-MAX * + CELLS JB-PIDS + ;






: PL-NULL-IN ( --- )   \ & 's begin (874, Rill's spawn, 813): a slot free, and /dev/null the first stage's stdin
