: R-RUN ( --- )
  \ Not INCLUDED: the boot word runs before the interpreter has a file
  \ to read from, and INCLUDED says "Error reading file" there; the
  \ program is read whole, its line ends made blanks, and EVALUATEd.
  SYS-ARGC 1 < IF R-REPL-D EXIT THEN                         \ no script: the prompt (824)
  0 SYS-ARG DUP CSTRLEN 2DUP R-RILL? >R R-SLURP 2DUP R-SHEBANG? R> OR IF R-COMPILE R-INSTALL ELSE R-BLANKS EVALUATE THEN ;   \ a .4: Forth
: R-INIT ( --- )
  \ What WARM and QUIT set before the interpreter reads - a boot word runs
  \ ahead of both, with the search order the build left (its wordlists'
  \ addresses from before the save), so EVALUATE there faulted.
  0 HANDLER !  DECIMAL  2 #ORDER !
  FORTH-WORDLIST CONTEXT !  FORTH-WORDLIST CONTEXT CELL+ !  FORTH-WORDLIST CURRENT !
  0 STATE !  TIB SRC !  0 SID !  INCLUDE-BUFFER INCLUDE-POINTER ! ;
\ ALLOC-BUFFERS first, as the shell's MAIN does: every BUFFER: (pool.4)
\ points into the heap of the session that built the image, gone at
\ the next run - shadow.4's LDECL-ADDRS among them, which is why a def
\ with locals, compiled after the load, wrote through a stale pointer
\ and faulted (Iteration 737). An error leaves with status 2.
\ R-RUN's xt kept as an offset (!XT): ['] in a definition compiles the
\ absolute address, which the save and reload leave pointing at nothing -
\ the CATCH that faulted at boot (Iteration 737), and why shell.4's
\ DO-FORTH keeps its EVALUATE the same way.
VARIABLE R-RUN-XT   ' R-RUN R-RUN-XT !XT
\ A trap in a script (818): a stack's guard page reached - recursion past what the stacks hold - is
\ Rill's error with its line, not the kernel's `relf: return stack overflow or data stack underflow`
\ and then `cm: error -5` with none. The engine restarts the VM on fresh stacks inside the runaway
\ region, so the frames R-WHERE reads are still there. Every other trap stays TRAPPED's.
: R-TRAP ( n --- )
  DUP -5 = OVER -3 = OR 0= IF TRAPPED EXIT THEN  DROP
  R-ERR> ." cm: recursion too deep for the stacks" R-ERR-NL
  HANDLER @ DUP DICT-LIMIT U> SWAP R0 @ U< AND 0= IF 2 SYS-EXIT THEN  -4004 THROW ;
VARIABLE R-TRAP-XT   ' R-TRAP R-TRAP-XT !XT
\ A def with locals saves them on the engine's save stack (4096 cells, LSAVE_MAX): some 2,000 levels
\ of its recursion fill it, and shadow.4's `shadow: save stack overflow` was followed by `cm: error -2`.
\ The engine calls the word at image offset 8 (shadow.4's LOCALS-FAILED); for Rill's image, this (818).
: R-LOCALS-FAILED ( n --- )
  1 = IF R-ERR> ." cm: recursion too deep for the stacks" R-ERR-NL -4004 THROW THEN
  R-ERR> ." cm: an engine fault - the locals' save stack underflowed" R-ERR-NL -4004 THROW ;
' R-LOCALS-FAILED START @ -   START @ 8 + !
: R-BOOT ( --- )
  ALLOC-BUFFERS  R-INIT  R-ARENA-INIT
  S" RILL_GC_STRESS" R-TEXT R-ENV @ IF -1 G-STRESS !  0 R-GC-AT ! THEN     \ a collection at every safe point: the tests' (776)
  0 R-ON-EXIT-XT !
  0 JB-N !  0 R-OUT-KEPT !  R-TRAP-XT @XT TRAP-XT!
  R-RUN-XT @XT CATCH ?DUP IF
    R-OUT-BACK  R-RUN-EXIT  R-JOBS-STOP               \ on EXIT runs however the script ends - to stdout (821); then its jobs stop (813)
    DUP -4000 = IF  DROP R-STATUS @ SYS-EXIT  THEN    \ a command failed, fail, exit: its status
    DUP -4100 -4000 WITHIN IF  DROP 2 SYS-EXIT  THEN    \ Rill's own errors: their message said already, with the line (781)
    R-ERR> ." cm: error " . R-NL  2 SYS-EXIT
