\ ---- The collector (Iteration 776) ---------------------------------------
\ Rill's values live in the arena, which only grew. At a safe point - between two statements of
\ the script's top level, where no value is held anywhere but in variables - once the arena has
\ grown past R-GC-AT, everything the registered variables reach is copied into a new arena, and
\ the old one is freed back to the system. The copy compacts: a list's items array is cut to its
\ count. The compilers register every variable of the script that can hold a text, a list, a
\ record or an item, and every top-level loop's source, with its kind (R-ROOT); a literal text
\ made once (gene littext) is kept outside the arena (R-FIX), as the regex cache's patterns are.
9 CONSTANT R-ITEM                                     \ an item variable's kind: compile.4's K-ANY

512 CONSTANT G-MAXROOTS
G-MAXROOTS CELLS BUFFER: G-RV   G-MAXROOTS CELLS BUFFER: G-RK   VARIABLE G-RN
: R-ROOT ( addr kind --- )
  G-RN @ G-MAXROOTS < 0= IF S" cm: too many variables to collect" R-FAIL THEN
  G-RK G-RN @ CELLS + !  G-RV G-RN @ CELLS + !  1 G-RN +! ;
VARIABLE G-OLD  VARIABLE G-END  VARIABLE G-TOP  VARIABLE G-BITS  VARIABLE G-RUNS  VARIABLE G-SIZE
: G-WHICH ( a --- entry | 0 )   \ the filled chunk holding a (918)
