: G-IN? ( a --- f )   DUP G-OLD @ U< 0= OVER G-END @ U< AND IF DROP -1 EXIT THEN  XN @ IF G-WHICH 0<> ELSE DROP 0 THEN ;
: G-BIT ( a --- byte-addr mask )
  DUP G-OLD @ U< 0= OVER G-END @ U< AND IF  G-OLD @ G-BITS @  ELSE  DUP G-WHICH DUP @ SWAP 2 CELLS + @  THEN   ( a base bits )
  >R - 3 RSHIFT  DUP 3 RSHIFT R> +  SWAP 7 AND 1 SWAP LSHIFT ;
: G-FWD? ( a --- f )   G-BIT SWAP C@ AND 0<> ;
: G-ALLOT ( n --- a )   7 + -8 AND  G-TOP @ SWAP OVER + G-TOP ! ;
: G-MOVE ( a n --- a' )   \ an object's n bytes into the new arena; the old place forwarded to it
  DUP G-ALLOT >R  OVER R@ ROT MOVE  R@ OVER !  G-BIT OVER C@ OR SWAP C!  R> ;
DEFER G-COPY ( a kind --- a' )
